---
description: How tests are written and named in Tadka
globs: tests/**/*.cs
alwaysApply: false
---

- xUnit, FluentAssertions, NSubstitute (never Moq, and only at an external boundary).
- Test names are readable snake case sentences, for example `Cancel_from_Created_succeeds_with_reason`.
- Integration tests use the existing fixtures (`TadkaApiFactory`, `RestaurantApiFactory`, `PaymentApiFactory`, `DeliveryApiFactory`). They start the database. Do not start your own container.
- Reuse `TestAuthHandler` and its `X-Test-*` headers for auth.
- Assert the response **and** the state (the row, or the `outbox_messages` row).
- Never weaken `tests/Tadka.Api.Tests/Architecture/BoundaryTests.cs` to make a change pass.
- Run your test with `dotnet test tests/<project> --filter "FullyQualifiedName~<Class>"`, then the whole project.
